  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $h(x),$ defined below?\n\n$$\nh(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-27,\\, & x<3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}\u2061(x-2),\\, & x\\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=3$\n- $h(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=3$\n- $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=3$",
  "worked_solution": "We're required to determine the left and right continuity properties of $h(x)$ at $x=3.$\n\nLet's start by computing $h(3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(3) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3-2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20611 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=3$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}h(x) & ={3}^{3}-27 \\\\  & =27-27 \\\\  & =0 \\\\  & =h(3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=3$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}h(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3-2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u20611 \\\\  & =0 \\\\  & =h(3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function is both left and right-continuous at $x=3,$ which implies that the function is continuous at $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
